# Keep the build context small and, more importantly, correct.
#
# The two that matter most:
#
#   data/     the SQLite database and every uploaded file. Copying it into the
#             image would bake one operator's content into a deployable layer
#             and, worse, ship it to anyone who pulls the image. The volume
#             mount is the only source of truth.
#   .env      real secrets. It must never reach the image, and it must never be
#             overridden by a COPY — a stale .env baked into a layer overrides
#             the platform's environment variables at runtime.

node_modules
dist
# Produced by the build inside the image. A stale local copy would only bloat the
# context; the image builds its own.
dist-server
data
# `npm run backup` output. Real content and documents — never in an image.
backups
.git
.gitignore

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

*.log
npm-debug.log*
coverage
.vite
*.tsbuildinfo

README.md
docs
